1
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
The most shocking tale of carnage ever seen.

2
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:00,000
House of 1000 Corpses is a horror film directed by Rob Zombie.

3
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Two teenage couples traveling across the backwoods of Texas searching for urban legends of serial
killers end up as prisoners of a bizarre and sadistic backwater family of serial killers.

4
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Captain Spaulding, played by Sid Haig.

5
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Otis B. Driftwood, played by Bill Moseley.

6
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Baby Firefly, played by Sheri Moon Zombie.

7
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Mother Firefly, played by Karen Black.

8
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Denise Willis, played by Erin Daniels.

9
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:09,000
Jerry Goldsmith, played by Chris Hardwick.

10
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
House of 1000 Corpses is a 2003 American black comedy horror film written, co-scored, and directed by
Rob Zombie in his directorial debut, and the first film in the Firefly film series.

11
00:48:57,000 --> 00:49:03,000
It stars Sid Haig, Bill Moseley, Sheri Moon, Karen Black, Rainn Wilson, Chris Hardwick, Tom Towles,
Erin Daniels, Jennifer Jostyn, Walton Goggins, and Dennis Fimple in his final role.

12
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
The plot centers on a group of teenagers who are kidnapped and tortured by a psychopathic
family during Halloween after traveling across the country to write a book.

13
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:57,000
Inspired by 1970s horror films such as The Texas Chain Saw Massacre (1974) and The Hills Have Eyes (1977), Zombie conceived the film while designing a
haunted-house attraction for Universal Studios Hollywood, where filming took place in 2000 on the backlots and in Valencia, California.

14
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:24,000
When the studio shelved the film fearing that it would receive
an NC-17 rating, Zombie re-acquired the rights.

15
01:06:45,000 --> 01:06:51,000
They were eventually sold to Lions Gate Entertainment,
who released the film in April 2003.

16
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
Despite receiving an unfavorable response from critics, it
went on to gross $16 million worldwide.

17
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:45,000
Since its release, the film has achieved a cult following, was developed into a haunted-house attraction by Zombie for
Universal Studios, and was followed by two sequels: The Devil's Rejects (2005) and 3 from Hell (2019).

18
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:12,000
The film explores themes of upper class, psychopath,
halloween, urban legend, satanic ritual.

19
01:24:33,000 --> 01:24:39,000
The tone is dark.
